# lazy-lock.json is deliberately NOT here: it is tracked.
#
# Untracked, every machine resolved plugin branches to whatever was current the
# day it last ran :Lazy update, so the same config ran on different plugin
# versions. That is not a theoretical drift — spring-boot.nvim changed its API
# between two machines' checkouts, Spring Boot LS stopped attaching to every
# .java file on one of them only, and the test suite could not reproduce it
# because the Mac had the older plugin. See CHANGELOG.md 2026-10-15.
#
# The cost is that `:Lazy update` now shows up as a diff. That is the point:
# a plugin version change becomes a reviewable commit instead of a silent
# difference between two laptops.

# Compiled Lua cache
*.luac

# Python bytecode — mcp/nvim_context_server.py, and py_compile in the test suite
__pycache__/

# Mason-installed binaries (reinstalled automatically)
/mason/

# Local/machine-specific overrides
local.lua
